        openings: ("A combine and two planters worth $140,000 were taken from rural farms in one night. Stripped GPS tags were found in {D}'s yard, {D}'s phone was near each farm, and no work orders exist for the machines.", "The defense evidence will establish that {D} is a working repairman, that customers confirm many repair jobs, and that no one saw {D} take any machine."),
        closings: ("$140,000 in machines gone from three farms in a night, stripped GPS tags in {D}'s yard, and {D}'s phone near each farm. No repair order explains any of it.", "A repairman with real customers and a phone that goes where the work is. The State must prove {D} took the machines, and no one saw {D} take anything."),
        timeline: [(-30, "The first farm."), (0, "Week 3: the second."), (0, "Week 4: the tags."), (1, "{DL} is arrested.")],
