        truths: ("{DL} had raised three other tenants' rent.", "{DL} sounded calm on the voicemail."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you threaten to call child services?", "\"No. I said I would make a call, and I meant a reminder about the rent.\""), .direct("Did you raise other tenants' rent?", "\"Yes, three others. It was normal. I did not single out {V.him}.\""), .direct("What was your relationship with {V}?", "\"{V} was a tenant for two years and usually paid late. I had raised the rent on three tenants that year.\""), .direct("What did you mean by the call?", "\"I meant it as a reminder that I would report problems at the home. I did not mean it as a threat.\""), .direct("Why did you say child services?", "\"I was frustrated and thought of the home conditions. It came out wrong.\""), .direct("How were things between you and {V} before that day?", "\"Mostly fine. {V} paid late a few times and I got frustrated. I should have sent a letter instead of leaving a voicemail.\""), .cross("You said 'pay or I make the call.' What call?", "\"I meant a call about the rent. I see how it sounds.\""), .cross("The lease has no $900 fee, does it?", "\"No. I thought there was a late fee. I should have checked.\""), .cross("You frightened {V} about {V.his} kids, didn't you?", "\"I did not mean to. I did not mention children in a threatening way. I truly am sorry.\""), .cross("The lease has no such fee, does it?", "\"No. I added it without telling anyone.\""), .cross("You asked for $900, didn't you?", "\"Yes, and I attached the call to the payment.\"")],
        openings: ("{D}, a landlord, left a voicemail telling {V} 'Pay or I make the call' about child services unless {V} paid $900, a fee that is not in the lease. {V} feared losing {V.his} kids.", "The defense witnesses will explain that {D} meant a call about rent or maintenance, spoke calmly, and never meant to threaten anyone's children."),
        closings: ("A voicemail that says 'Pay or I make the call,' a $900 fee that the lease does not contain, and a tenant afraid of losing {V.his} kids. {D} used fear to get paid.", "A calm landlord who meant a call about rent. The State must prove {D} threatened to report {V}, and the voicemail never says it."),
        timeline: [(-10, "The fee dispute."), (0, "6 p.m.: the voicemail."), (0, "6:30 p.m.: {V} saves it."), (1, "{V} reports.")],
        identified: "A voicemail.",
        aggravating: ["The defendant took advantage of a position of trust or confidence"],
        mood: .sympathetic,
        impact: "I was scared to answer the door.",
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"])

    static let caretakerSavingsMoveV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.caretakerSavingsMove",
        category: .whiteCollar,
        headlines: ["Home Aide Added Her Name to Retired Teacher's Account", "Statements Show Weekly Withdrawals"],
        law: "exploitationElder",
        threshold: 8,
        spec: "Exploited a disabled adult by deception, obtaining $26,000, on or about {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "{V}, a retired teacher with memory loss, lost $26,000 over five months after {D}, a home aide, was added to {V.his} account on {DATE}. {DL} says {V} asked for the help.",
        state: [E(.document, 3, "Bank Statements", "Weekly withdrawals by {D}."), E(.document, 3, "Signature Card", "{D} added in the same week."), E(.statement, 2, "Niece", "'He didn't know what he signed.'")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Asked", "{DL} says {V} asked for help.")],
        role: "Niece",
        exam: [.direct("How are you related to {V}?", "\"I'm {V}'s niece. {V} is a retired teacher who never had children of {V.his} own and taught half the people in this town.\""), .direct("What condition is {V} in?", "\"{V} has memory loss. There are good days, but on others {V} does not know what month it is or what {V.he} had for breakfast.\""), .direct("When did {D} come into {V}'s life?", "\"{D} was hired as a home aide. About five months before {DATE}, {D} was added to {V}'s bank account in the same week.\""), .direct("What did you notice about the account?", "\"Weekly withdrawals in round amounts, always made by {D}. The bank statements showed the same pattern every week for five months.\""), .direct("How much was taken?", "\"$26,000 in five months. That was most of the savings {V} spent a career as a teacher building up, and I was horrified when I added it.\""), .direct("What did you do?", "\"I asked the bank for an audit. After the audit confirmed the withdrawals, I went to the Sheriff's Office with the statements.\""), .cross("Did you see {D} take the money?", "\"No. I only saw the bank statements and the signature card. I did not watch any withdrawal happen.\""), .cross("Did {V} ever say {V.he} asked {D} for help?", "\"{V} said something like that once to me, but {V} also forgets what {V.he} says from one hour to the next.\""), .cross("Were you at the bank when {D} was added?", "\"No. I live out of town, and I only learned about the card after I got the statements.\""), .cross("Did {V} sign the signature card?", "\"Yes. {V}'s signature is on it. I do not believe {V} understood what adding {D} meant.\""), .cross("How often did you visit {V}?", "\"Every few weeks. It was not often enough, and I will carry that for a long time.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Bank teller",
        defenseExam: [.direct("What is your job at the bank?", "\"I'm a teller. I have worked at this branch for eleven years, and I handle deposits, withdrawals, and new account cards.\""), .direct("Do you remember {V}?", "\"Yes. {V} has been a customer for decades and taught my own children. I remember {V} coming in once with an aide.\""), .direct("What happened that day?", "\"{D} and {V} came in to add {D} to the account. I went through the signature card with {V} and explained what it meant.\""), .direct("Did {V} appear to understand?", "\"{V} nodded and smiled and said something like, yes, that's fine. {V} signed the card in front of me at the window.\""), .direct("Did you have any concerns at that moment?", "\"Not at that moment. {V} seemed pleasant and engaged, and there was nothing about the visit that raised a flag for me.\""), .direct("Did the bank have any alerts on the account?", "\"No. The withdrawals were in normal round amounts, and nothing tripped our system until the niece asked for the audit.\""), .cross("Did you assess {V}'s memory that day?", "\"No. That is not our role, and I'm not trained for it. I only watched whether {V} signed willingly.\""), .cross("Did you see {V} sign the card?", "\"Yes. I watched {V} sign it myself, and I witnessed it.\""), .cross("Would you have noticed memory loss?", "\"It's possible, if it had been obvious. It was not obvious to me that day.\""), .cross("Did you speak with {D}?", "\"Briefly, to complete the paperwork. {D} was polite and let {V} do the talking.\""), .cross("Did the bank notice the weekly withdrawals before the audit?", "\"No. They were not flagged, and nobody at the branch connected them until the niece called.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} drained an account.", "Asked for help."),
        allocution: "\"I thought I was helping.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} bought furniture with the money.", "The bank teller recalls {V} nodding."),
        defendant: [.direct("What was your job?", "\"I was a home aide for {V}. I cooked, cleaned, drove {V} to appointments, and helped with paying the monthly bills.\""), .direct("How did you get added to the account?", "\"{V} asked me to help with the bills. We went to the bank together, and {V} signed the card in front of the teller.\""), .direct("What was the money for?", "\"Some of it was household costs. I bought groceries, paid for a plumbing repair, and covered the pharmacy bills out of the account.\""), .direct("What about the rest of it?", "\"I bought furniture for my own place. I know I should not have used {V}'s money for that, and I have no excuse.\""), .direct("Did {V} know about the withdrawals?", "\"{V} knew I was taking money out for bills. {V} was warm and trusting with me, and I took advantage of that trust.\""), .direct("What would you say now?", "\"That I made a terrible mistake. I let {V}'s trust turn into something I used, and I am ashamed.\""), .cross("You withdrew $26,000, didn't you?", "\"Over five months, yes. I have seen the statements, and the total is accurate.\""), .cross("You used some of it on furniture, didn't you?", "\"Some of it, yes. I am not going to hide that from this court.\""), .cross("{V} has memory loss, doesn't {V.he}?", "\"Yes. I knew that when I took the job, and I knew it every week I took money.\""), .cross("You never told {V}'s niece about the withdrawals, did you?", "\"No. I did not tell anyone in the family, and That is on me.\""), .cross("The signature card was signed the same week you were hired, wasn't it?", "\"About that time, yes. It was within the first week or two of my working there.\"")],
        openings: ("{V}, a retired teacher with memory loss, lost $26,000 over five months after {D}, a home aide, was added to {V.his} account. The statements show weekly withdrawals by {D}, and the signature card was added the same week. {V}'s niece found it during an audit.", "{D} says {V} asked for help with bills, and a bank teller recalls {V} nodding when {D} was added. {D} was warm and trusted. The State must prove {D} took money {V} did not agree to give."),
        closings: ("A teacher with memory loss, a home aide with access, and $26,000 gone in five months. The statements show every withdrawal. {V} trusted {D} completely.", "A bank teller saw {V} nod and agree to the signature card. {V} asked for help. The State must prove that {V} did not consent to these withdrawals."),
        timeline: [(-150, "{DL} is added."), (0, "Month 5: the audit."), (0, "Month 5: the niece."), (1, "{DL} is charged.")],
        identified: "Bank statements.",
        aggravating: ["The victim was particularly vulnerable", "The defendant took advantage of a position of trust or confidence"],
        mood: .wantsConviction,
        impact: "She trusted her completely.",
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"],
        genders: ["D": .female, "V": .male])

    static let custodyExchangeFlightV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.custodyExchangeFlight",
        category: .violent,
        headlines: ["Mother Drives Off With Child From Visitation Center", "Phone Pings Two States Away"],
        law: "kidnapping2",
        threshold: 7,
        spec: "Unlawfully took and carried away {V}, a minor, without consent of the lawful custodian, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "{D}, the noncustodial mother, left a visitation center with {V}, a six-year-old, on {DATE}. The court order allowed supervised visits only. {DL} says {D.he} feared for {V.him}.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Lot Camera", "{D} buckles {V} into a car."), E(.document, 3, "Order", "Supervised visits only."), E(.digital, 2, "Phone Ping", "The phone two states away.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Fear", "{DL} says {D.he} feared for {V}.")],
        role: "Center supervisor",
        exam: [.direct("What is your role at the visitation center?", "\"I'm the center supervisor. I oversee the supervised visits, check in the parents, and make sure a staff member is in the room for the whole visit.\""), .direct("What did the court order say about {D}'s visits with {V}?", "\"It allowed supervised visits only, at our center, for one hour, with a staff member present. {D} was not permitted to take {V} out of the building or off the grounds.\""), .direct("What happened on {DATE}?", "\"{D} arrived at about 4 p.m. for the visit with {V}, who is six. The first twenty minutes looked ordinary, with a staff member in the room.\""), .direct("What did the parking lot camera show?", "\"At about 4:20, {D} walks out the side door holding {V}'s hand and buckles {V} into the back seat of a car. {D} then gets in and drives away.\""), .direct("What did you do?", "\"I called the Sheriff's Office within minutes and gave the plate and the direction of travel. I also called the other parent, who was waiting for the exchange.\""), .direct("What happened afterward?", "\"The next day {D}'s phone pinged two states away. On day two, {V} was found safe and returned, and a deputy told me where.\""), .cross("Was {V} crying or resisting when {D} walked out?", "\"Not that I could see on the video. {V} walked alongside {D} and did not pull away. I wouldn't call it a struggle.\""), .cross("Did {D} ever tell you {D.he} was worried about {V}'s safety?", "\"Not that day, and not in any visit I supervised. {D} was polite and quiet at check-in.\""), .cross("Where was the staff member when {D} left the room?", "\"Stepping out to answer a front desk call. That was a lapse on our side, and I have changed the procedure since.\""), .cross("Did {V} appear healthy and well cared for at the visits?", "\"As far as I could see, yes. I'm not a social worker, and I have no way to see what happens at either home.\""), .cross("Did {D} hurt or threaten {V}?", "\"No. The video shows {D} holding {V}'s hand. I never saw {D} raise a voice at {V} or anyone else.\"")],
        defenseRole: "School teacher",
        defenseExam: [.direct("What is your job at {V}'s school?", "\"I teach first grade. {V} was in my class that year, and I saw {V} every morning and afternoon.\""), .direct("How would you describe {V} in class?", "\"Bright, quiet, and a little guarded. {V} loves books, draws well, and tends to watch the room before joining in.\""), .direct("Did {V} ever say anything about home?", "\"Once, during a drawing activity, {V} told me nights were cold at the house and described a blanket. I wrote it down but did not know what to make of it.\""), .direct("Did you report that conversation?", "\"I mentioned it to the school counselor, who said they would watch for more. Nothing else came of it before the visitation incident.\""), .direct("How did {V} act when {D} was mentioned?", "\"{V} lit up. {V} spoke warmly about {D} and kept a photo in a notebook. I never saw fear of {D}.\""), .direct("What did you hear after the incident?", "\"The school sent a notice that {V} was found safe. {V} returned to class a week later and seemed relieved to see familiar faces.\""), .cross("Did {V} say who kept the house cold?", "\"No. {V} didn't say whose home or why. It was a passing remark, and I did not ask follow-up questions that day.\""), .cross("Did you see any signs of neglect, like missing meals or dirty clothes?", "\"No. {V} came to school clean, fed, and on time. I never saw a bruise or anything I would be required to report.\""), .cross("Did you speak with {D} about {V}'s worries?", "\"Never. I have met {D} once at a conference, briefly, and we did not discuss anything like that.\""), .cross("Would a parent be allowed to remove a child from supervised visitation?", "\"No. Not without a court's permission. A concern like this goes to the school counselor or the court.\""), .cross("Did you tell the court or social services what {V} said?", "\"I did not go to the court. I told the counselor, and I assume the counselor handled the rest.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} took a child.", "Fear."),
        allocution: "\"I wasn't thinking.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} filed no emergency motion.", "{V} told a teacher about cold nights."),
        defendant: [.direct("Why did you leave the center with {V}?", "\"I was frightened for {V}. I had come to believe {V} was not safe in the other home, and I felt there was nobody listening to me.\""), .direct("What did you fear?", "\"{V} had told me about cold nights and being left alone. I did not know what to do with that, and the visits were only an hour.\""), .direct("What were you thinking when you walked out?", "\"I wasn't thinking in a straight line. I just wanted to get {V} somewhere warm and safe, and I let that take over.\""), .direct("Did you plan the trip beforehand?", "\"I'd been thinking about it for weeks, but I did not map out a route. I got in the car and drove, and I turned my phone off for part of it.\""), .direct("How was {V} while you were together?", "\"{V} was calm and curious. We talked in the car, and I tried to keep things normal and gentle, so {V} wouldn't be scared.\""), .direct("What happened when {V} was found?", "\"{V} was returned to the other parent. I told the deputies why I did it. I know I broke the court's order, and I understand how it looks.\""), .cross("The order said supervised visits only, didn't it?", "\"Yes, it did. I read it many times. I knew that leaving the center broke it.\""), .cross("You walked out while the supervisor was away from the room, didn't you?", "\"The staff member had stepped out, and I took the chance. I'm not proud of that.\""), .cross("You drove two states away, didn't you?", "\"Yes. My phone pinged in another state, and I'm not going to argue about where I went.\""), .cross("You never called the other parent or the court to say where {V} was, did you?", "\"No. I did not call anyone. I was scared and thought I'd explain later.\""), .cross("{V} is six years old and could not agree to go anywhere, could {V.he}?", "\"No. A six-year-old goes where the adult goes. I understand that this made me responsible.\"")],
        openings: ("The court allowed {D} only supervised visits with {V}, a six-year-old, at a visitation center. On {DATE}, while the staff member stepped away, {D} walked {V} out, buckled {V} into a car, and drove off, and {D}'s phone pinged two states away the next day. The lot camera and the order tell the story.", "{D} acted out of fear for a six-year-old who had told a teacher that nights at home were cold. {D} did not hurt or frighten {V}, who walked out holding {D.his} hand. You will hear from the teacher who heard the comment and what {D} said when {V} was found."),
        closings: ("A court order for supervised visits only, a six-year-old walked to a car, and a phone two states away. {D} knew the order and left anyway, and never called anyone. The video shows it all.", "A frightened parent and a child who spoke of cold nights to a teacher. {D} never struck or threatened {V}, and {V} was returned safely. The State must prove {D} acted without any belief that {V} was in danger."),
        timeline: [(0, "4 p.m.: the visit."), (0, "4:20 p.m.: the lot."), (1, "The phone pings."), (2, "{V} is found.")],
        identified: "A camera.",
        aggravating: ["The victim was particularly vulnerable"],
        mood: .divided,
        impact: "I thought she was gone.",
        doctrines: ["necessity", "lesserIncluded"],
        genders: ["D": .male, "V": .male])

    static let rooftopPharmacyBreakInV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.rooftopPharmacyBreakIn",
        category: .property,
        headlines: ["Vent Cut at Rural Clinic, Opioid Cabinet Emptied", "Alarm Silenced From Outside"],
        law: "burglary2",
        threshold: 7,
        spec: "Broke and entered a building, a clinic owned by {V}, with intent to commit larceny, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "A rural clinic's rooftop vent was cut on {DATE} and $11,000 in opioids was taken. A saw blade in {D}'s truck matched. {DL} says {D.he} sold the saw weeks earlier.",
        state: [E(.physical, 3, "Saw Blade", "Matches the cut.", .search), E(.video, 2, "Roof Camera", "A hooded figure."), E(.document, 2, "Inventory", "$11,000 missing.")],
        defense: [E(.document, 1, "Receipt", "A saw sale receipt.")],
        role: "Clinic manager",
        exam: [.direct("What was taken from your clinic in the break-in?", "\"$11,000 in opioids. A rooftop vent was cut open, and a hooded figure appears on the roof camera.\""), .direct("What matched the cut in the vent?", "\"A saw blade found in {D}'s truck during a search. The blade matches the cut in the vent.\""), .direct("What does your inventory show after the break-in?", "\"$11,000 in opioids missing. We counted every bottle after the break-in, and the count is in the report.\""), .direct("What did you find at the clinic?", "\"A rooftop vent cut open with a saw, and the pharmacy room below ransacked. $11,000 in opioids was missing from the locked cabinet.\""), .direct("What did the roof camera show?", "\"A hooded figure working at the vent at 2 a.m. and leaving with a bag. The face was not visible.\""), .direct("How was {D} connected?", "\"A saw blade in {D}'s truck matched the cuts in the vent. {D} is a roofer who works in the county.\""), .cross("{D} says {D.he} sold the saw weeks before, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"A receipt names a buyer for the saw. I will say that the receipt exists, and I have seen it.\""), .cross("Can you identify the hooded figure on your roof camera?", "\"No. The hood covers the face, and the picture is too small and dark to tell who it is.\""), .cross("Did anyone see {D} on the clinic roof that night?", "\"No. I have no witness who saw {D} on the roof, and I did not see anyone myself.\""), .cross("Many roofers use the same blades, don't they?", "\"They do. The match was on the cut pattern and the blade type.\""), .cross("{D} said the saw was sold weeks earlier, didn't {D.he}?", "\"Yes, and a receipt names a buyer. We have not located the buyer.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Roofer",
        defenseExam: [.direct("Did {D} buy tools from your supply business?", "\"Often. {D} bought saws and blades from my supply, and we worked together on a number of roofing jobs.\""), .direct("Was this particular saw one that {D} bought from you?", "\"Maybe. I sold {D} several saws over time, and I do not recall the details of each one.\""), .direct("Did {D} ever resell tools to other people?", "\"Sometimes. {D} sold some tools to others when {D} did not need them, and I saw that happen.\""), .direct("How do you know {D}?", "\"We work on the same crews. I have known {D} for years.\""), .direct("What do you know about the saw?", "\"I saw {D} sell it weeks before to another roofer. They talked about the price.\""), .direct("What kind of person is {D}?", "\"Reliable on the job. {D} has struggled with pills but is trying to stay clean.\""), .cross("Do you know who bought this saw from {D}?", "\"No. I do not know who bought it. I was not there for that sale and never saw the buyer.\""), .cross("Was {D} working on any roof job with you that week?", "\"Not with me. I do not know where {D} was working that week, or whether {D} had any job at all.\""), .cross("Do you know whether {D} used pills during that time?", "\"I have heard that. I do not know it for a fact, and I would not want to guess.\""), .cross("You did not see the sale paperwork, did you?", "\"No. I only saw them shake hands.\""), .cross("{D} had a history with pills, didn't {D.he}?", "\"Yes. I know that.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} cut into a clinic.", "A sold saw."),
        allocution: "\"I'm ashamed.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} had used pills.", "The receipt names a buyer."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you break into the clinic?", "\"No. I never went to that clinic or cut that vent. I was not there.\""), .direct("What about the saw blade in your truck?", "\"I sold the saw weeks earlier. The blade stayed in the truck by mistake.\""), .direct("Who bought the saw?", "\"A buyer with a receipt. I have the receipt that names the buyer.\""), .direct("What do you do for a living?", "\"I am a roofer. I use a reciprocating saw and replace blades often.\""), .direct("What happened to the saw?", "\"I sold it weeks before to another roofer I know from jobs. I have a receipt naming the buyer.\""), .direct("Why was a blade in your truck?", "\"I keep old blades in a bin. I never gave them a second thought.\""), .cross("The blade in your truck matches the cut, doesn't it?", "\"So they say. A blade like mine could cut that. I did not use it.\""), .cross("You had used pills yourself, hadn't you?", "\"I took pills. It was a separate matter.\""), .cross("Why was the blade in your truck if you sold the saw?", "\"I forgot to remove it. I kept some blades.\""), .cross("You have used pills, haven't you?", "\"Yes, in the past. I have been working on that.\""), .cross("You work on roofs, don't you?", "\"Yes. That is why this looks like it fits.\"")],
        openings: ("A rural clinic's rooftop vent was cut and $11,000 in opioids taken. A hooded figure appears on the roof camera, and a saw blade in {D}'s truck matches the cut.", "Weigh the defense proof, which will show that {D} sold the saw weeks earlier, that a receipt names the buyer, and that no one saw {D} on that roof."),
        closings: ("A cut in a rooftop vent, a matching saw blade in {D}'s truck, and $11,000 in opioids gone. {D} knew those pills.", "A saw sold weeks earlier with a receipt for the sale. The State must prove {D} was the figure on the roof, and a blade in a truck is not proof."),
        timeline: [(-14, "The saw sale."), (0, "2 a.m.: the vent."), (0, "7 a.m.: the manager."), (1, "The blade.")],
        identified: "A saw blade.",
        aggravating: ["The offense was committed for pecuniary gain"],
        mood: .wantsConviction,
        doctrines: ["searchSeizure"])

    static let hospitalBillingIdentityV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.hospitalBillingIdentity",
        category: .whiteCollar,
        headlines: ["Pharmacy Clerk Opens Store Cards in Customers' Names", "Same Terminal, Nine Customers"],
        law: "identityTheft",
        threshold: 7,
        spec: "Knowingly obtained identifying information of {V} and used it to obtain credit, on or about {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "Eight customers got store card bills they never opened after {D}, a pharmacy clerk, copied information on {DATE}. {DL} says a manager's login was shared.",
        state: [E(.digital, 3, "Terminal Log", "Eight lookups at {D}'s terminal."), E(.document, 3, "Applications", "Mailed to a rented box."), E(.document, 2, "Box Rental", "The box was {D}'s.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Shared", "{DL} says logins were shared.")],
        role: "Pharmacy manager",
        exam: [.direct("What is your role at the pharmacy?", "\"I'm the pharmacy manager. I supervise the clerks and technicians, run the terminal permissions, and handle the audit reports when something looks off.\""), .direct("How did this problem first come to your attention?", "\"Eight customers called to say they'd received bills for a store credit card they never applied for. Each of them had filled a prescription with us in recent weeks.\""), .direct("What did the terminal log show?", "\"Eight lookups of those customers' records at {D}'s terminal, starting about two weeks before the first card was mailed. The log records the login and the time.\""), .direct("What does a lookup give a person at the terminal?", "\"Name, date of birth, address, and the last digits of identifying numbers. It's the same screen used to verify who is picking up a prescription.\""), .direct("What happened to the credit card applications?", "\"They were mailed to a rented postal box, not to the customers' homes. The card company traced each application to the same box.\""), .direct("Whose box was it?", "\"The rental records show the box was {D}'s. That is what connected the lookups at the terminal to the applications.\""), .cross("Is it true that clerks sometimes share logins?", "\"I've found that some did, which I'm not proud of. We had a note with passwords on a shelf, and I've changed that policy since.\""), .cross("Did anyone else use {D}'s terminal?", "\"It's a shared counter. Other clerks and technicians could have used that terminal when {D} stepped away.\""), .cross("Did you review the camera footage at the counter?", "\"We have a camera over the register, not the terminal screen. I did not match the lookup times to who stood there.\""), .cross("Did {D} ever complain about the shared passwords?", "\"I don't recall that. {D} was never flagged for problems before this.\""), .cross("How long did the customers take to fix their credit?", "\"Some of them took close to a year. I know that from the calls we got, and I take that seriously.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Pharmacy tech",
        defenseExam: [.direct("What is your job at the pharmacy?", "\"I'm a pharmacy tech. I fill prescriptions, answer the phone, and cover the counter when it's busy.\""), .direct("How does logging in work?", "\"Each of us has a login, but the system times out quickly. To avoid constantly retyping, people started sharing a few passwords, kept on a note by the register.\""), .direct("Did you use other people's logins?", "\"Yes, sometimes. When the counter was busy, I used whichever terminal was open and whichever password was handy.\""), .direct("Did {D} share the login too?", "\"I believe everyone did. It was common knowledge where the note was kept, and no one thought much about it.\""), .direct("Did the manager know about the note?", "\"I think so. It was in plain sight on a shelf by the register for months.\""), .direct("Did you ever see {D} look up customers inappropriately?", "\"No. I never saw {D} do anything like that. {D} was fast and friendly with customers.\""), .cross("Did you look up those eight customers?", "\"No. I did not. I'd remember if I had.\""), .cross("Do you know who did?", "\"I do not. I only know the passwords were widely shared.\""), .cross("Did you see anyone with the credit card applications?", "\"No. I never saw any applications or any mail like that.\""), .cross("Did {D} ever rent a postal box?", "\"I don't know about {D}'s personal arrangements. We never talked about it.\""), .cross("Did the shared passwords let anyone see any record?", "\"Yes. Anyone logged in could pull any customer's information.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} stole customers' identities.", "Shared logins."),
        allocution: "\"I'm so sorry.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} rented the box.", "Passwords were on a note."),
        defendant: [.direct("What was your job at the pharmacy?", "\"I worked the front counter as a clerk. I rang up purchases, checked in prescriptions, and answered questions.\""), .direct("Did you look up those eight customers?", "\"My login shows lookups, but I did not run those searches myself. We were all using the same few passwords written on a note near the register.\""), .direct("Who knew the password?", "\"Everyone at the counter. The note sat by the register, and techs used whichever terminal was free.\""), .direct("Do you rent a postal box?", "\"Yes. I use one for my own mail and packages. I did not use it for any credit card applications.\""), .direct("How could applications reach your box?", "\"I do not know. I'm not sure whether someone gave my box number on the forms, but I did not collect any applications myself.\""), .direct("What did you do when the manager asked you about it?", "\"I told the manager I did not know how the lookups were made and I offered to help sort it out.\""), .cross("The lookups were made under your login, weren't they?", "\"They show my login. I'm not arguing about what the log says. I'm saying other people could use it.\""), .cross("The box belongs to you, doesn't it?", "\"Yes, I rent it. It is in my name, and I'm not hiding that.\""), .cross("Eight customers' applications went to your box, didn't they?", "\"That is what I'm told. I do not know how that happened.\""), .cross("You never reported anyone using your login, did you?", "\"No. I did not know it was being used. If I had, I would have said something.\""), .cross("You had access to every one of those customers' records, didn't you?", "\"At the counter, I had access to anyone's record, as did the other clerks.\"")],
        openings: ("Eight customers received store credit card bills they never applied for after {D}, a pharmacy clerk, looked up their information at a terminal. The lookups were made under {D}'s login, and the applications were mailed to a postal box that {D} rents. The records tie each step to {D}.", "Passwords at this pharmacy sat on a note by the register, shared by the whole counter, and the log shows only a login, not a person. {D} rents a postal box for ordinary mail, and nothing links {D}'s hands to those applications. You will hear a technician describe the note."),
        closings: ("Eight lookups under {D}'s login, eight applications mailed to {D}'s box, and eight customers who spent up to a year clearing their names. The pharmacy's records follow the information straight to {D}. That is identity theft by someone entrusted with the records.", "A password note by the register and a counter full of people who knew it: the log shows a login, not a face. The camera was never matched to the lookup times. The State must prove {D} was the one who used the information."),
        timeline: [(-14, "Lookups begin."), (0, "Week 2: cards mailed."), (0, "Week 3: bills."), (1, "{DL} is arrested.")],
        identified: "Terminal logs.",
        aggravating: ["The defendant took advantage of a position of trust or confidence"],
        mood: .wantsConviction,
        impact: "It took a year to fix.",
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"])

    static let tavernTruckShotsV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.tavernTruckShots",
        category: .violent,
        headlines: ["Gunfire Hits Roadhouse Sign and Front Windows at Closing", "Casings Left on Gravel Lot"],
        law: "dischargingOccupied",
        threshold: 7,
        spec: "Willfully discharged a firearm into an occupied building, a roadhouse owned by {V}, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "Five shots hit a roadhouse's front windows on {DATE} as patrons left. {D}'s pistol matched the casings. {DL} says the pistol was stolen.",
        state: [E(.forensic, 3, "Casings", "Match {D}'s pistol."), E(.video, 2, "Lot Camera", "A car leaves the gravel lot."), E(.document, 2, "Banned Notice", "{D} was banned weeks earlier.")],
        defense: [E(.document, 1, "Theft Report", "The pistol reported stolen days before.")],
        role: "Roadhouse owner",
        exam: [.direct("Who is {D} to your roadhouse?", "\"{D} was banned weeks earlier. I have the banned notice.\""), .direct("What happened at your roadhouse?", "\"About 1 a.m., five shots hit the front windows as patrons were leaving. Glass shattered across the porch, and everyone dove for cover.\""), .direct("What did your lot camera show?", "\"A car leaving the gravel lot right after the shots. The camera did not catch a plate.\""), .direct("What do you know about {D}?", "\"I banned {D} weeks earlier after a fight. The casings from the scene matched {D}'s pistol.\""), .direct("What did you do when the shots hit the windows?", "\"I told everyone to get down and kept them away from the glass. I dialed 911 as soon as the second shot came through.\""), .direct("What damage did the shots cause to the building?", "\"Five windows were shattered and a neon sign was hit. The repair came to about $3,000 and we closed for two days.\""), .cross("{D} says the pistol was stolen, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"A theft report was filed after the shooting. I will say so.\""), .cross("Did you see the shooter?", "\"No. It was dark, and I did not see who fired.\""), .cross("Was anyone hurt?", "\"No. The shots hit the windows. No one was hit.\""), .cross("Nobody was hit, were they?", "\"No one was hurt. Several people were close to the windows.\""), .cross("{D} reported the pistol stolen, didn't {D.he}?", "\"Yes, days after the shooting. I think that timing matters.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Neighbor",
        defenseExam: [.direct("Was {D}'s car at home on the night of the shooting?", "\"I think so. I saw it in the driveway at some point in the evening, parked where it usually is.\""), .direct("Was {D}'s car there all night long?", "\"No. I did not see it all night. I only saw it earlier in the evening, before I went to bed.\""), .direct("Did you see {D} at home that evening?", "\"I saw the car, not {D}. I did not see {D} that evening, so I cannot say who was inside.\""), .direct("How do you know {D}?", "\"I am a neighbor and see {D} often. {D} lives a few houses away.\""), .direct("What did you see that night?", "\"Nothing. I was in bed and heard nothing from {D}'s house.\""), .direct("What do you know about the pistol?", "\"{D} told me it was stolen. I did not see the pistol before.\""), .cross("Did you see the car leave the driveway that night?", "\"No. I went to bed and did not watch the street, so I cannot say if it left or not.\""), .cross("Was the car still there when you woke up in the morning?", "\"I did not look. I do not know, and I would be guessing if I said it was or was not.\""), .cross("How far is {D}'s house from the roadhouse where this happened?", "\"A few miles. It is a short drive down the county road, maybe ten minutes at night.\""), .cross("You do not know when {D} reported it, do you?", "\"I heard days later.\""), .cross("You do not know where {D} was at 1 a.m., do you?", "\"I assume home, but I cannot say.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} shot a roadhouse.", "A stolen pistol."),
        allocution: "\"Nobody was meant to be hurt.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} reported the theft after the shooting.", "{DL}'s phone was home."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you shoot at the roadhouse windows?", "\"No. I did not fire any shots. I was not at the roadhouse that night, and I stayed at home.\""), .direct("Whose pistol fired the casings that were found?", "\"Mine, but it was stolen days before the shooting. I did not notice it was missing until afterward.\""), .direct("When did you report the pistol stolen to deputies?", "\"After the shooting. I did not notice it was gone until deputies asked me about it that day.\""), .direct("How did you lose the pistol?", "\"It was taken from my truck a few days before. I did not notice right away.\""), .direct("When did you report it?", "\"After I heard about the shooting. I should have reported it sooner.\""), .direct("Where were you that night?", "\"At home. My phone was home, and I was asleep.\""), .cross("You were banned from the roadhouse weeks earlier, weren't you?", "\"Yes. I was angry about it. But I would never shoot at a building full of people over a ban.\""), .cross("You reported the theft only after the shooting, didn't you?", "\"Yes. That was the first time I checked for it. I wish I had noticed it was gone sooner.\""), .cross("The pistol that fired those shots was yours. How is that not you?", "\"Someone took it and used it. I did not. I know how it looks, but I did not do it.\""), .cross("You were banned from that roadhouse, weren't you?", "\"Yes, after an argument. I was angry about it.\""), .cross("The casings match your pistol, don't they?", "\"So I was told. I cannot explain it beyond the theft.\"")],
        openings: ("Five shots hit a roadhouse's front windows as patrons left, and the casings match {D}'s pistol. {D} had been banned from the roadhouse weeks earlier.", "The defense evidence will establish that the pistol was stolen before the shooting and that no one saw {D} at the roadhouse that night."),
        closings: ("Five shots into a roadhouse as patrons left, casings from {D}'s own pistol, a car leaving the lot, and a ban weeks earlier. The pieces all point to {D}.", "A pistol stolen before the shooting and a theft reported late. The State must prove {D} fired it, and a stolen gun in someone else's hands does not prove that."),
        timeline: [(-30, "{DL} is banned."), (0, "1 a.m.: the shots."), (0, "1:10 a.m.: the lot."), (1, "The match.")],
        identified: "Casings.",
        aggravating: ["The offense involved a firearm"],
        mood: .wantsConviction,
        doctrines: ["alibi"])

    static let fishPlantGhostPayrollV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.fishPlantGhostPayroll",
        category: .whiteCollar,
        headlines: ["Warehouse Payroll Lead Added Phantom Night Shift", "Direct Deposits to Two Accounts"],
        law: "embezzlement100k",
        threshold: 8,
        spec: "Embezzled over $100,000 belonging to {V}, a distribution warehouse, by a person in a position of trust, on or about {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "A distribution warehouse lost $118,000 over two years to a phantom night shift. {D}, the payroll lead, approved each time sheet on {DATE}. {DL} says a supervisor added the names.",
        state: [E(.document, 3, "Time Sheets", "Eight phantom workers."), E(.document, 3, "Direct Deposits", "Two accounts tied to {D}'s family."), E(.digital, 2, "Approval Log", "{D}'s approvals.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Supervisor", "{DL} says a supervisor added the names.")],
        role: "Warehouse controller",
        exam: [.direct("What is your role at the warehouse?", "\"I'm the controller. I oversee payroll, the books, and the reconciliations. When numbers do not match, they come to my desk.\""), .direct("What did you discover about the night shift?", "\"Over about two years, the warehouse paid roughly $118,000 to eight workers on a night shift who never appeared on the floor. They were phantoms.\""), .direct("How did you find that out?", "\"During an audit, I matched time sheets against badge scans and the dock logs. Eight names had paychecks and approved hours but no badge swipes and no work.\""), .direct("Who approved those time sheets?", "\"{D}, the payroll lead. The approval log shows {D}'s sign-off on every one of those sheets, week after week.\""), .direct("Where did the money go?", "\"Direct deposit records show two of the accounts are tied to {D}'s family. The bank confirmed the account holders when we asked.\""), .direct("What was the effect on the warehouse?", "\"We had to cut a shift after the loss was discovered. People who did real work lost hours so we could absorb the hit.\""), .cross("Did anyone besides {D} have access to add names to the payroll system?", "\"Yes. A night supervisor had the ability to submit new hires and time entries. I did not audit that access before the discovery.\""), .cross("Were the names entered by {D} or by someone else?", "\"The log shows the sign-off by {D}, but the original entries came through the supervisor's queue. I did not look at who typed them.\""), .cross("Did you check the supervisor's badge activity?", "\"I looked at the floor badge scans. I did not compare the supervisor's badge times with the entry times in detail.\""), .cross("Did {D} ever raise any concern about the night shift?", "\"No. {D} never flagged anything, but I do not know whether {D} was aware of the phantoms.\""), .cross("Were the family accounts in {D}'s name?", "\"Two accounts were tied to {D}'s family, not in {D}'s own name. I don't know how involved {D} was in opening them.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Night supervisor",
        defenseExam: [.direct("What is your job at the warehouse?", "\"I'm a night supervisor. I run the floor from ten to six, assign tasks, and submit the time entries for my crew.\""), .direct("Did you add workers to the night shift?", "\"I submitted names for new hires and temps when they arrived. That is part of my job.\""), .direct("Did you add those eight names?", "\"I do not recognize those names as people I submitted. I don't know where they came from.\""), .direct("Did you ever see the badge scans?", "\"Yes. I see them for my crew. I did not see scans for those eight names.\""), .direct("Where were you at 2 a.m. on some of those nights?", "\"On the floor, usually, and my badge scanned in the warehouse. That's the pattern the controller found.\""), .direct("What would it take to enter a name?", "\"Access to the payroll queue. I have it, and so does {D}, and so do the controller and the HR clerk.\""), .cross("Did you enter any of those names?", "\"I don't believe I did. I can't swear to each entry, but I did not knowingly submit a phantom.\""), .cross("Did you ever notice someone on your shift you didn't know?", "\"No. I know everyone on my crew. I'd know a stranger.\""), .cross("Who else had access to the queue?", "\"Several people. I couldn't list them all.\""), .cross("Did {D} ask you about the names?", "\"Not that I recall. {D} just approved what came in.\""), .cross("Did you stay late on any of those nights?", "\"Sometimes. My badge shows 2 a.m. scans on several of them.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} paid ghost workers.", "A supervisor."),
        allocution: "\"I regret everything.\"",
        truths: ("{DL}'s brother owned an account.", "The supervisor's badge scanned at 2 a.m."),
        defendant: [.direct("What was your job?", "\"I was the payroll lead. I reviewed time sheets, approved them for processing, and answered questions from employees.\""), .direct("How did you approve the night shift sheets?", "\"They came to me already filled out by the night supervisor. I approved what was in front of me and did not check each name against a roster.\""), .direct("Did you know the eight workers?", "\"No. I did not know them personally. I assumed they were night crew I'd never met.\""), .direct("Who entered the names?", "\"A night supervisor submitted them. I'm not the person who created those entries.\""), .direct("Do you know the accounts tied to your family?", "\"I know a relative's account was among them, but I did not know the deposits were coming from payroll.\""), .direct("What would you do differently?", "\"Check every name against a real person. I trusted the sheets, and I should not have.\""), .cross("You approved every one of those time sheets, didn't you?", "\"Yes. The log shows my sign-off. I'm not disputing that.\""), .cross("You never met a single one of those eight workers, did you?", "\"No. I never saw them, and I should have noticed that.\""), .cross("A relative's account received those deposits, didn't it?", "\"So I'm told. I did not ask where the money came from.\""), .cross("Two years of approvals is a long time to miss that, isn't it?", "\"It is, and that's what haunts me. I was busy and I trusted the supervisor.\""), .cross("You never asked the controller for a roster, did you?", "\"No. In hindsight, yes. It would have caught this.\"")],
        openings: ("For two years, a distribution warehouse paid $118,000 to eight night shift workers who never worked. {D}, the payroll lead, approved every time sheet, and direct deposits for two of the phantom workers went to accounts tied to {D}'s family. You will hear from the controller who found them.", "{D} approved the sheets that were put in front of {D}, and a night supervisor's queue is where the names came from. A supervisor will tell you who had access to add them. The State must prove {D} knew the workers were not real."),
        closings: ("Eight workers no one has ever met, two years of approvals with {D}'s sign-off, and deposits that landed in accounts tied to {D}'s family. $118,000 went out the door. The warehouse had to cut a shift.", "The names came through a supervisor's queue, and the supervisor's badge scanned at 2 a.m. on nights the phantoms were paid. The controller never compared those badge times in detail. An approval is not proof that {D} created the workers."),
        timeline: [(-700, "The first phantom."), (0, "Year 2: the audit."), (0, "Year 2: the deposits."), (1, "{DL} is suspended.")],
        identified: "Time sheets.",
        aggravating: ["The defendant took advantage of a position of trust or confidence", "The offense was committed for pecuniary gain"],
        mood: .wantsConviction,
        impact: "We cut a shift.",
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"])

    static let countyFuelDepotSkimV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.countyFuelDepotSkim",
        category: .property,
        headlines: ["Highway Garage Loses Diesel Overnight for Months", "Hidden Tank Behind Shed"],
        law: "felonyLarceny",
        threshold: 7,
        spec: "Stole diesel fuel valued at $17,000 belonging to {V}, a county, on or about {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "A highway garage lost 4,500 gallons over months. A hidden tank behind {D}'s shed held matching dye. {DL} says it was for a loader.",
        state: [E(.physical, 3, "Hidden Tank", "A tank with county dye.", .search), E(.document, 3, "Inventory", "4,500 gallons missing."), E(.video, 2, "Garage Camera", "{D}'s truck at night.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Loader", "{DL} says it was for a loader.")],
        role: "County finance officer",
        exam: [.direct("What is your role with the county?", "\"I'm the finance officer. I review the budgets, the inventory counts, and the audits for the departments, including the highway garage.\""), .direct("What did you find at the highway garage?", "\"The inventory showed about 4,500 gallons of fuel missing over roughly four months, with purchases matching deliveries but the tanks coming up short.\""), .direct("How did you trace it?", "\"I started an audit and asked deputies to look at where the fuel might have gone. Cameras at the garage showed a truck coming at night.\""), .direct("What does the garage camera show?", "\"{D}'s truck pulling up to the pump area at night, more than once, with the lights off. The camera times line up with some of the shortages.\""), .direct("What was found at {D}'s property?", "\"Behind {D}'s shed, a hidden tank with dye in the fuel matching the county's dye. The dye is used to mark off-road diesel owned by the county.\""), .direct("What was the value of the fuel?", "\"Roughly 4,500 gallons at the county's cost. It's a significant loss for a small garage, and it came out of the road budget.\""), .cross("Could county fuel have gone into a county loader legitimately?", "\"Yes. The county has a loader that uses off-road diesel. It was fueled twice during that period, which is in the records.\""), .cross("Did {D} have authority to fuel county equipment?", "\"As a road foreman, {D} could authorize fueling for county equipment. I do not know whether {D} had authority to move fuel to a private tank.\""), .cross("Did the dye prove the fuel came from the garage?", "\"It shows the fuel is dyed like the county's. Other agencies and farms also use dyed diesel, so it is not exclusive.\""), .cross("How many people had access to the pumps at night?", "\"The garage staff had keys. Some of them are on the camera in the early morning. I did not get a list of every key holder.\""), .cross("Did anyone see {D} fill the tank?", "\"No. We have the truck on camera, but no one watched {D} put fuel into the hidden tank.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Road foreman",
        defenseExam: [.direct("What is your job with the county?", "\"I'm a road foreman, like {D}. We share crews on big jobs, and I know the garage and its equipment.\""), .direct("How do you fuel the loader?", "\"From the garage pump, at the start of a shift. The loader holds about a hundred gallons and burns fast during plowing.\""), .direct("Did the county ever let foremen keep fuel at their sheds?", "\"It has happened informally during storms, so a crew can get out early. There is no written policy that I know of.\""), .direct("How many times did the loader get fueled in that period?", "\"Twice that I know of. I helped once. It's a regular machine and not a thirsty one.\""), .direct("Did you know about {D}'s tank?", "\"I knew {D} had a small tank for the loader. I did not know how big it was.\""), .direct("Did you see {D} at the garage at night?", "\"A couple of times. {D} said {D.he} was getting an early start.\""), .cross("Did you see {D} take large amounts of fuel?", "\"No. I did not see how much {D} took.\""), .cross("Did you ever fill {D}'s tank?", "\"No. I only saw {D} at the pump.\""), .cross("Is the loader big enough to need thousands of gallons?", "\"Not in months. It uses a few hundred, at most.\""), .cross("Did anyone sign off on moving fuel?", "\"I never saw anything in writing.\""), .cross("Did you talk to {D} about it later?", "\"Briefly. {D} was upset and said it was for work.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} took county fuel.", "A loader."),
        allocution: "\"I thought no one would notice.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} filled the tank at night.", "The loader was fueled twice."),
        defendant: [.direct("What was your job with the county?", "\"I was a road foreman, in charge of a crew that maintains the county roads and equipment.\""), .direct("Why was a tank behind your shed?", "\"I kept fuel for a loader I use for county work, to get an early start in bad weather.\""), .direct("Where did the fuel come from?", "\"Some of it was fuel I authorized from the garage for the loader. I did not realize it was being taken from county supply for private use.\""), .direct("Why did you pull in at night?", "\"I started early on snow days and early spring work. I fueled the loader after hours to be ready.\""), .direct("Did you take 4,500 gallons?", "\"No. The loader does not use anywhere near that. It was fueled twice during that period.\""), .direct("What did you tell the finance officer?", "\"That the tank was for a loader, and that I'd be glad to show the records. I did not hide it.\""), .cross("The tank behind your shed was filled with county-dyed fuel, wasn't it?", "\"That is what the test showed. I had dyed fuel from the garage for the loader.\""), .cross("Your truck was on the garage camera at night, wasn't it?", "\"Yes. I went at night so I wouldn't interfere with the day crew.\""), .cross("A loader does not need thousands of gallons, does it?", "\"Not for the work I did, no. But I'm not the one who counted what was left in the tank.\""), .cross("You didn't ask permission to store fuel at home, did you?", "\"I did not ask in writing. I thought it was understood.\""), .cross("You never recorded the fuel you moved, did you?", "\"I wrote down some, and not all. That's my mistake.\"")],
        openings: ("A county highway garage lost about 4,500 gallons of fuel over four months. A truck matching {D}'s appears on the garage camera at night, and a hidden tank behind {D}'s shed held fuel with the county's dye. You will hear from the finance officer who ran the audit.", "{D} kept fuel for a county loader and fueled it at night to get an early start on bad weather. A fellow foreman will tell you this was an informal practice. The State must prove {D} took far more than a loader could use."),
        closings: ("Months of shortages, a truck at the garage at night, and a hidden tank behind {D}'s shed with county dye. {D} was a foreman with the keys. 4,500 gallons came out of the road budget.", "A loader was fueled twice and foremen informally kept fuel to start early. No one watched {D} fill the hidden tank, and the dye is not unique to this county. The State must prove {D} intended to take county fuel for private use."),
        timeline: [(-120, "Fuel drops."), (0, "Month 4: the audit."), (0, "Month 4: the tank."), (1, "{DL} is suspended.")],
        identified: "A hidden tank.",
        aggravating: ["The defendant took advantage of a position of trust or confidence"],
        mood: .wantsConviction,
        doctrines: ["searchSeizure"])

    static let stagedCrashClaimV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.stagedCrashClaim",
        category: .whiteCollar,
        headlines: ["Two Cars, One Body Shop: Rear-End Claim Raises Flags", "Same Chiropractor, Same Wording"],
        law: "insuranceFraud",
        threshold: 7,
        spec: "Presented a false claim to an insurer, {V}, seeking $36,000 for a staged collision, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "{D} claimed $36,000 after a low-speed rear-end collision on {DATE} with a car repaired at the same body shop. Both drivers used one chiropractor. {DL} says it was bad luck.",
        state: [E(.document, 3, "Claim Files", "Identical injury wording."), E(.document, 3, "Shop Records", "Both cars at one shop."), E(.video, 2, "Camera", "A tap at five mph.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Luck", "{DL} says it was bad luck.")],
        role: "Insurance investigator",
        exam: [.direct("What did you notice about {D}'s claim?", "\"{D} claimed $36,000 after a low-speed rear-end collision. The injury wording is identical in both drivers' claim files.\""), .direct("What else linked the two drivers?", "\"Both cars were repaired at the same body shop, and both drivers used the same chiropractor.\""), .direct("What did you notice about the claims?", "\"Two claims from one tap, with nearly identical injury wording. Both claimants used the same chiropractor and the same body shop.\""), .direct("What did the camera show?", "\"A tap at about five miles per hour at 3 p.m. There was barely any contact.\""), .direct("How much was claimed?", "\"$36,000 in total, mostly for treatment and a rental. The injuries did not match the damage.\""), .direct("What did you do after you saw the two claims side by side?", "\"I pulled both files and compared the wording. The paragraphs were almost word for word the same, so I sent them to our fraud unit.\""), .cross("{D} says it was bad luck, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"Many customers use the shop. I will say that is true.\""), .cross("Did {D} pay the shop in cash?", "\"I understand so. I did not see the payment.\""), .cross("Were the injuries real?", "\"The chiropractor documented injuries. I cannot say how serious.\""), .cross("Many people use the same shop, don't they?", "\"Yes. That is why I looked at the pattern.\""), .cross("The shop did legitimate repairs, didn't it?", "\"I did not find fault with the repairs.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Body shop owner",
        defenseExam: [.direct("Do your customers share a chiropractor in town?", "\"Many do. We recommend one nearby, and most of our customers go there after a crash for a checkup.\""), .direct("Are two crashes in one week involving your shop common?", "\"Rare, but it can happen. Many people in town bring their cars to us, so the overlap is not impossible.\""), .direct("Did {D} pay for the repair in cash at your shop?", "\"Yes. {D} paid cash. Many of our customers pay cash for repairs, and we give a receipt each time.\""), .direct("What do you do?", "\"I own the body shop where both cars were repaired. We repair many vehicles each week.\""), .direct("How did {D} pay?", "\"In cash, which is common. We gave a receipt.\""), .direct("What did you see of the crash cars?", "\"Minor bumper damage. It was nothing unusual.\""), .cross("Do you know the other driver in that collision well?", "\"Not well. The other driver was also a customer, but I had no connection beyond the repair.\""), .cross("Did you see the crash itself at any point?", "\"No. I only saw the cars after they were brought in. I cannot say how the crash really happened.\""), .cross("Do you get a referral fee when customers go to the chiropractor?", "\"No. I do not get a fee. I only suggest a place that is close and that customers like.\""), .cross("You referred customers to a chiropractor, didn't you?", "\"Sometimes, when they ask.\""), .cross("Two cars from one tap at your shop is a coincidence, isn't it?", "\"I do not control who is in a crash.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} staged a crash.", "Bad luck."),
        allocution: "\"I made a bad decision.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} paid the shop in cash.", "Many customers use the shop."),
        defendant: [.direct("Was the crash with the other car staged?", "\"No. It was bad luck. I was hit in a low-speed rear-end collision, and I was hurt afterward.\""), .direct("Why did both cars go to the same body shop and chiropractor?", "\"Both are near my home and popular in town. I did not choose them to match the other driver.\""), .direct("Did you pay the body shop in cash for the repair?", "\"Yes. I paid cash. I prefer to pay cash when I can, and the shop gave me a receipt.\""), .direct("What happened in the crash?", "\"I was rear-ended at low speed while stopped in traffic. My neck felt stiff the next morning.\""), .direct("Why did you use that shop and chiropractor?", "\"A friend recommended them. I paid the shop in cash.\""), .direct("What do you say about the claim?", "\"I was hurt and filed what the doctor suggested. I did not plan any of it.\""), .cross("The injury wording is identical in both claims, isn't it?", "\"The chiropractor writes it that way. It is not my wording, and I did not write the claim file myself.\""), .cross("$36,000 for a five-mile-an-hour tap. Isn't that a lot of money?", "\"I was hurt. The doctor documented the injuries, and the claim reflects the treatment I needed.\""), .cross("You and the other driver used the same shop. Don't you know each other?", "\"No, I do not. It is a coincidence. I never met the other driver before the crash.\""), .cross("The other driver used the same chiropractor, didn't {V.he}?", "\"Apparently. It was a coincidence.\""), .cross("A five mile an hour tap is minor, isn't it?", "\"Yes, and I did not expect to be hurt.\"")],
        openings: ("{D} claimed $36,000 after a five-mile-an-hour rear-end tap. Both cars were repaired at the same body shop, both drivers used one chiropractor, and the injury wording is identical.", "The defense witnesses will explain that many customers use that shop and that chiropractor, and that {D} was hurt in a real collision."),
        closings: ("A five-mile-an-hour tap, a $36,000 claim, the same body shop, the same chiropractor, and identical wording in both files. That is a staged crash.", "A real crash, a popular shop, and a doctor who documented injuries. The State must prove {D} planned the collision, and it has only a coincidence of choices."),
        timeline: [(-14, "The shop referral."), (0, "3 p.m.: the tap."), (1, "The claims."), (30, "The flag.")],
        identified: "Claim files.",
        aggravating: ["The offense was committed for pecuniary gain"],
        mood: .divided,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"])

    static let diningWitnessThreatV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.diningWitnessThreat",
        category: .violent,
        headlines: ["Man Whispers Warning to Witness at Courthouse Elevator", "Camera Catches the Moment"],
        law: "witnessIntimidation",
        threshold: 7,
        spec: "Threatened {V}, a witness, to deter testimony in a pending case, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "{D} stepped into an elevator with {V}, a witness, on {DATE} and told {V.him} to 'think about home.' {DL} says it was small talk.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Elevator Camera", "{D} leans close to {V}."), E(.statement, 3, "Witness", "'He said think about home.'"), E(.document, 2, "Subpoena", "{V} was subpoenaed.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Small Talk", "{DL} says it was small talk.")],
        role: "Bailiff",
        exam: [.direct("What is your role at the courthouse?", "\"I'm a bailiff. I keep order in the courtrooms, escort witnesses and jurors, and watch the hallways and elevators on trial days.\""), .direct("Who is {V}?", "\"A witness in a pending case, subpoenaed three days before {DATE}. {V} was scheduled to testify in a trial that week.\""), .direct("What happened on the morning of {DATE}?", "\"At about 9 a.m., {D} stepped into an elevator with {V}. The elevator camera shows {D} leaning close to {V} and speaking quietly.\""), .direct("What did {V} tell you?", "\"At 9:05, {V} came to me, visibly shaken, and said that {D} had told {V.him} to think about home. {V} was rattled and had a hard time standing still.\""), .direct("Why did that matter?", "\"{V} was about to testify, and {D} was connected to the defendant in that case. A comment like that in an elevator, to a witness, is taken seriously.\""), .direct("What did you do?", "\"I wrote down what {V} said, secured the area, and informed the court. {D} was arrested later that day.\""), .cross("Did {D} say anything threatening in plain words?", "\"According to {V}, the words were think about home. There was no threat of violence in those exact words.\""), .cross("Could you hear what {D} said in the elevator?", "\"No. The elevator camera has no audio. I only know what {V} told me and what the video shows.\""), .cross("Did {D} touch {V}?", "\"No. The video shows {D} standing close and speaking, but there was no contact.\""), .cross("Did {V} know {D} before that morning?", "\"I understand they were acquainted. I heard they had met at church, though I do not know how well.\""), .cross("Did {V} testify?", "\"{V} almost didn't, but did. I do not want to say more than that.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Court clerk",
        defenseExam: [.direct("What is your role at the courthouse?", "\"I'm a court clerk. I work on the second floor and ride the same elevators as the lawyers, jurors and witnesses.\""), .direct("Do you know {D} and {V}?", "\"I recognize both. They have attended the same church as my family, and I have seen them greet each other on Sundays.\""), .direct("How did they usually act toward each other?", "\"Friendly. They nodded and chatted briefly, like acquaintances. I never saw any tension between them.\""), .direct("How crowded are the elevators on trial mornings?", "\"Packed. Sometimes five or six people squeeze in, and you end up face to face with strangers.\""), .direct("Do people in the elevator talk?", "\"Quite a bit. Small talk about the weather, the parking, the long hearings. It's a way to ease nerves.\""), .direct("Did you hear what {D} said that morning?", "\"No. I was on a different floor. I only heard about it from the bailiff.\""), .cross("Were you in the elevator?", "\"No. I was not there. I can't speak about what was said.\""), .cross("Did you see the video?", "\"I saw part of it, without sound. It showed two people standing very close.\""), .cross("Did you know {V} was a witness?", "\"I knew a witness had been subpoenaed. I did not know it was {V}.\""), .cross("Did {D} ever say anything to you about the case?", "\"No. {D} did not discuss it with me.\""), .cross("Do you know where {V} lives?", "\"Roughly, from church. Nothing more.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} threatened a witness.", "Small talk."),
        allocution: "\"I was scared.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} knew where {V} lived.", "They had met at church."),
        defendant: [.direct("Why were you at the courthouse that morning?", "\"I came to watch a hearing for someone I know. I did not go there to find {V}.\""), .direct("How did you end up in the elevator with {V}?", "\"We got in at the same time on the first floor. It was crowded, and we ended up next to each other.\""), .direct("Did you know {V}?", "\"I knew {V} from church. We had said hello for years, and I knew {V} lived on the east side of town.\""), .direct("What did you say?", "\"I said something like, you must be nervous, think about home, meaning go home and relax after. I meant it kindly.\""), .direct("Did you mean to threaten {V}?", "\"No. It was small talk. I would never threaten anyone, least of all someone I see on Sundays.\""), .direct("Why did you lean close?", "\"The elevator was packed, and I could hardly hear. I leaned in to be heard, and that's all.\""), .cross("You knew {V} was a witness, didn't you?", "\"I'd heard it. Everyone in the church knew. I did not talk about the case.\""), .cross("You knew where {V} lived, didn't you?", "\"In general terms, yes. It's a small community.\""), .cross("You said think about home, didn't you?", "\"Yes, I said that. I did not hear how it could sound until later.\""), .cross("You were connected to the defendant in {V}'s case, weren't you?", "\"I know the defendant, yes. That's why I was at the courthouse.\""), .cross("{V} reported it within five minutes, didn't {V.he}?", "\"Yes. {V} was upset. I understand why now.\"")],
        openings: ("Three days after being subpoenaed, {V} stepped into a courthouse elevator with {D}, who leaned close and told {V} to think about home. The elevator camera shows {D} bending toward {V}, and {V} reported it within five minutes. You will hear from the bailiff who took the report.", "{D} and {V} know each other from church, and the words in the elevator were small talk in a packed car. A court clerk who sees them every Sunday will describe how friendly they have always been. The State must prove {D} meant the words as a threat."),
        closings: ("A witness, an elevator, and a quiet sentence about home from someone who knew where {V} lived. {V} reported it within minutes and almost did not testify. The camera shows {D} leaning close.", "Think about home is not a threat of violence, and the elevator camera has no sound. {D} and {V} have greeted each other at church for years. The State must prove the words were meant to frighten."),
        timeline: [(-3, "{V} is subpoenaed."), (0, "9 a.m.: the elevator."), (0, "9:05 a.m.: {V} reports."), (1, "{DL} is arrested.")],
        identified: "A camera and a witness.",
        aggravating: ["The offense involved a threat"],
        mood: .wantsConviction,
        impact: "I almost didn't testify.",
        doctrines: ["relevance"],
        genders: ["D": .male])

    static let highSchoolPostThreatV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.highSchoolPostThreat",
        category: .violent,
        headlines: ["Student Posts Photo of Rifle With Caption About Homecoming", "School Cancels Dance"],
        law: "massViolenceThreat",
        threshold: 7,
        spec: "Threatened to commit mass violence on educational property, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: false,
        summary: "A photo of a rifle with a caption about homecoming appeared on {DATE}. The account belonged to {D}. {DL} says the photo was from a hunting trip.",
        state: [E(.digital, 3, "Post", "A rifle photo with a threat caption."), E(.digital, 3, "Account Records", "The account belonged to {D}."), E(.document, 2, "Search", "A rifle in the home.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Hunting", "{DL} says the photo was from hunting.")],
        role: "Detective",
        exam: [.direct("What was your assignment in this case?", "\"I'm a detective. I was assigned on {DATE} after a photo of a rifle with a caption about homecoming appeared on a social media account.\""), .direct("What did the post show?", "\"A rifle on a bed, with a caption about what would happen at homecoming. It was posted at about 6 p.m. and spread quickly among students.\""), .direct("What happened after the post?", "\"By 7 p.m. the school and the Sheriff's Office were getting reports. The next day the homecoming dance was cancelled.\""), .direct("How did you identify the account?", "\"The platform's account records show the account belonged to {D}, with {D}'s phone number and email attached.\""), .direct("What did you find at {D}'s home?", "\"A search turned up a rifle in the home. I'm not saying it is the same rifle as in the photo, but it was similar.\""), .direct("What did you do?", "\"I interviewed {D}, who said the photo was from a hunting trip. I arrested {D} two days after the post.\""), .cross("Did {D} write the caption?", "\"The caption was posted from {D}'s account. I do not have evidence of who typed it, but the account is {D}'s.\""), .cross("Was the rifle in {D}'s home a hunting rifle?", "\"It was a bolt-action rifle of the kind used for deer. It was not an assault-style weapon.\""), .cross("Did you find any plan for the homecoming dance?", "\"No. I found no notes, no maps, no messages about the dance. Only the post.\""), .cross("Did {D} threaten anyone by name?", "\"The caption did not name a person. It referenced homecoming, which is why the school was alarmed.\""), .cross("Did {D} delete the post?", "\"I believe the post was taken down after a few hours. I do not know who removed it.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Hunting buddy",
        defenseExam: [.direct("How do you know {D}?", "\"We hunt together every fall. I've known {D} for about six years, and we share a camp in the mountains.\""), .direct("Do you remember the photo?", "\"Yes. It was taken at our cabin last year before opening day. The rifle was on a bunk, and I'm in the next shot.\""), .direct("What kind of rifle is it?", "\"A bolt-action deer rifle. {D} has had it for years and uses it for hunting only.\""), .direct("What kind of person is {D}?", "\"Quiet, a little goofy. {D} makes bad jokes, but I've never seen {D} be violent or talk about hurting people.\""), .direct("Did {D} talk about the post?", "\"Afterward, yes. {D} said it was a joke about fireworks and that {D.he} regretted it.\""), .direct("Did {D} plan anything for homecoming?", "\"No. {D} did not even plan to go. We were going to hunt that weekend.\""), .cross("Were you with {D} when the post was written?", "\"No. I wasn't there. I only saw it after it was up.\""), .cross("Did you know the caption was changed?", "\"I didn't know that until afterward.\""), .cross("Do you know how the rifle was stored?", "\"In a locked case at {D}'s house, as far as I know.\""), .cross("Did {D} text you about the dance?", "\"No. Not about that.\""), .cross("Would you describe the joke as harmless?", "\"I would not. I understand why it scared people.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} threatened a school.", "A hunting photo."),
        allocution: "\"I never meant it.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} had changed the caption that day.", "The rifle was a hunting rifle."),
        defendant: [.direct("Where was the photo taken?", "\"On a hunting trip with a friend the previous fall. I took it in a cabin before heading out for deer.\""), .direct("Why did you post it?", "\"I was joking around with friends. I changed the caption that afternoon to something I thought was funny and didn't think it through.\""), .direct("What did the caption say?", "\"Something about homecoming being a blast. I meant it as a dumb joke about fireworks, not about hurting anyone.\""), .direct("Did you plan to do anything at the dance?", "\"No. I wasn't even going. I had no plan and I never meant to threaten anyone.\""), .direct("What did you do when you heard about the reports?", "\"I took it down. I was shaken, and I understood how it must have looked to the school.\""), .direct("What do you say to the students?", "\"I am truly sorry. It was a stupid joke that scared people.\""), .cross("The post said homecoming, didn't it?", "\"Yes. That was the word. I didn't realize how it would be read.\""), .cross("You changed the caption the same day, didn't you?", "\"Yes, I edited it that afternoon before I posted.\""), .cross("The rifle in your home is similar to the one in the photo, isn't it?", "\"Yes. It's the same hunting rifle I used last fall.\""), .cross("The dance was cancelled because of the post, wasn't it?", "\"That's what I've been told. I feel terrible.\""), .cross("You didn't think about how a rifle and homecoming would sound together, did you?", "\"No. I did not. That was careless.\"")],
        openings: ("On {DATE}, a photo of a rifle with a caption about homecoming appeared on an account that belongs to {D}. The school received reports within the hour, and the dance was cancelled. Account records tie the post to {D}, and a similar rifle was in {D}'s home.", "{D} took the photo on a hunting trip a year earlier and wrote a clumsy joke about fireworks. A hunting buddy will tell you about the cabin, the rifle, and {D}'s quiet, goofy nature. The State must prove {D} meant to threaten the school."),
        closings: ("A rifle, a caption about homecoming, an account in {D}'s name, and a dance cancelled by fear. {D} changed the caption that afternoon and posted it. That is a threat to a school.", "A hunting rifle in a cabin photo from last fall, no plan, no notes, no messages about the dance. {D} took the post down and apologized. A bad joke is not a threat unless the State proves it was meant as one."),
        timeline: [(0, "6 p.m.: the post."), (0, "7 p.m.: reports."), (1, "The dance is cancelled."), (2, "{DL} is arrested.")],
        identified: "A post.",
        mood: .divided,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"])

    static let bridgeRescueAssaultV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.bridgeRescueAssault",
        category: .violent,
        headlines: ["Person Kicks Trooper Pulling Them From Highway Overpass Edge", "Body Camera Footage Released"],
        law: "assaultLEO",
        threshold: 6,
        spec: "Assaulted {V}, a law enforcement officer performing official duties, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "On {DATE}, trooper {V} grabbed {D} from an overpass edge. {D} kicked {V}, breaking a rib. {DL} says {D.he} was in crisis.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Body Camera", "{D} kicks the trooper."), E(.forensic, 2, "Medical Report", "A cracked rib."), E(.statement, 2, "Motorist", "A uniformed trooper and lights.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Crisis", "{DL} says {D.he} was in crisis.")],
        role: "Trooper",
        exam: [.direct("What is your job?", "\"I'm a state trooper. On {DATE} I was on the night patrol when a call came in about a person on the edge of an overpass.\""), .direct("What time did you arrive?", "\"The call was around 11 p.m., and I reached the overpass within a few minutes. I saw {D} standing on the outer edge of the rail.\""), .direct("What did you do?", "\"I activated my lights, approached slowly, and talked with {D}. At about 11:10, when I thought {D} was about to step off, I grabbed {D} and pulled {D.him} back.\""), .direct("What happened when you grabbed {D}?", "\"{D} kicked me hard in the ribs. I felt it crack. I held on and got {D} over the rail while a motorist stopped.\""), .direct("What did the body camera show?", "\"The kick, clearly, at 11:11. It shows me grabbing {D}, the struggle, and {D} lashing out with a foot.\""), .direct("What was your injury?", "\"A cracked rib. I was taken to the ER at about 11:30 and kept for observation. I was off duty for several weeks.\""), .cross("Did {D} seem to know you were helping?", "\"I don't think so. {D} was crying and in the middle of a crisis. I'm not sure {D} was thinking at all.\""), .cross("Did {D} say anything to you before you grabbed {D.him}?", "\"{D} said something about not wanting to be a burden. I tried to keep {D} talking, and then I made my move.\""), .cross("Did you know a hotline had called 911?", "\"I learned later that a hotline counselor had called. I was dispatched based on that call.\""), .cross("Was the kick intentional or a reflex?", "\"It was a hard kick. I can't tell what was in {D}'s mind. It could have been a panic reaction.\""), .cross("Did {D} try to hurt you after you got {D.him} over the rail?", "\"No. Once we were on the ground, {D} stopped fighting and cried. I stayed with {D} until the ambulance came.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Hotline counselor",
        defenseExam: [.direct("What do you do?", "\"I'm a crisis hotline counselor. I answer calls from people in distress and, when necessary, I call emergency services.\""), .direct("Do you recall the call on {DATE}?", "\"Yes. A caller said they were on an overpass and could not go on. I stayed on the line and kept talking.\""), .direct("What did you do?", "\"I called 911 on a second line and gave the location. I kept the caller engaged until I heard sirens.\""), .direct("How did the caller sound?", "\"Exhausted, tearful, and very quiet. The caller spoke in short sentences and said sorry a lot.\""), .direct("Did the caller sound aware of surroundings?", "\"Not fully. The caller spoke in a fog, like someone barely tracking what was happening around them.\""), .direct("How do crises like that affect people?", "\"They can cause tunnel vision. A person can react physically without understanding who is touching them.\""), .cross("Did you hear the kick?", "\"No. The call dropped when the trooper arrived. The news of it reached me from the trooper's office the next day.\""), .cross("Did you know the caller's name?", "\"The caller gave a first name. I did not record the rest. I'm not sure I could identify {D}.\""), .cross("Did the caller say anything about hurting anyone else?", "\"No. Nothing like that.\""), .cross("Did the caller leave a note?", "\"The caller mentioned having left one at home. I passed that to dispatch.\""), .cross("Were you at the overpass?", "\"No. I was in my office. I only know the call.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} kicked a trooper.", "A crisis."),
        allocution: "\"I should have walked away.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} had left a note.", "A hotline called 911."),
        defendant: [.direct("Why were you on the overpass?", "\"I was in the worst place I have ever been. I felt there was no way forward, and I had left a note at home.\""), .direct("What do you remember of the officer?", "\"Lights, a voice talking to me, and a hand grabbing me. I remember panic more than anything.\""), .direct("Why did you kick?", "\"I didn't understand what was happening. I felt someone grabbing me, and my body just reacted. It was not a decision.\""), .direct("Did you mean to hurt the trooper?", "\"No. I did not even register that it was a trooper. I was fighting for balance and fighting off being grabbed.\""), .direct("What happened after?", "\"I was taken to the hospital and kept for a few days. I started treatment, and I'm still in it.\""), .direct("Looking back, how do you feel about it now?", "\"Grateful that I'm alive, and sorry that I hurt someone who was trying to save me.\""), .cross("The body camera shows you kicking the trooper, doesn't it?", "\"Yes. I've watched it. It's hard to see, and I apologize.\""), .cross("You heard the trooper identify as law enforcement, didn't you?", "\"I heard a voice. In my state, I'm not sure I understood.\""), .cross("The trooper cracked a rib, didn't the trooper?", "\"I've been told so. I would never want that.\""), .cross("You left a note before going to the overpass, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I left it at home. It's part of why I know how serious it was.\""), .cross("You kept struggling until you were over the rail, didn't you?", "\"Part of it. Then I stopped. I'm not sure how long.\"")],
        openings: ("On the night of {DATE}, a trooper grabbed {D} from the edge of an overpass, and {D} kicked the trooper hard enough to crack a rib. The body camera records the kick at 11:11. You will hear from the trooper about the rescue and the injury.", "{D} was in a mental health crisis and had left a note at home. A hotline counselor called 911 to save {D}'s life, and the kick was a panicked reaction to being grabbed in the dark. The State must prove {D} meant to hurt anyone."),
        closings: ("A trooper pulled a person back from a fall, and {D} kicked hard enough to crack a rib on camera. The trooper spent weeks off duty. {D} knew a person was grabbing {D.him}.", "A person in the worst moment of life, a note left at home, and a kick that was a reflex to being grabbed. The counselor describes a fog of crisis. The law distinguishes a deliberate assault from a panicked reaction."),
        timeline: [(0, "11 p.m.: the call."), (0, "11:10 p.m.: the grab."), (0, "11:11 p.m.: the kick."), (0, "11:30 p.m.: the ER.")],
        identified: "A body camera.",
        mitigating: ["The defendant was suffering from a mental condition that reduced culpability"],
        mood: .sympathetic,
        doctrines: ["insanity", "lesserIncluded"],
        genders: ["D": .male])

}
